  "claim_boundary": "E137 proves the real wait and queue-submit shapes and their service-side costs during one completed native-resolution run. The Wait-only ANR guard acted during the benchmark, so 7.1 FPS is not a clean optimization result. Direct mapped device memory remains an untested hypothesis, and removing the measured mirror cost alone cannot explain or close the full gap to the roughly 31-FPS direct path."
